From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: lusoris <lusoris@proton.me>
Date: Sat, 17 Oct 2026 19:33:49 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] avfilter/vf_tonemap_opencl: add the bt2408_hable tone map

Run the bt2408_hable tone map of vf_tonemap on the GPU. The host fills
the same FFBT2408Hable state as the CPU filter (the Hable lookup table
on PQ intensity, the IPT matrices and the black lift) and uploads it as
a constant buffer when the peak or the input primaries change. The
kernel in opencl/bt2408_hable.cl is a line by line port of the per-pixel
part of bt2408_hable.c and writes P010 or NV12 directly, with the chroma
taken from the encoded values like a software scaler does.

The output is always in BT.709 primaries and the light level and
mastering display side data is removed, since the frames are SDR.

On 10 frames of a 2160p HDR10 clip the GPU output differs from the CPU
tonemap=bt2408_hable path by a mean CIEDE2000 of 0.18 (95th percentile
0.98) and from vf_libplacebo with tonemapping=hable by 0.72. Four frames
of a 720p Dolby Vision profile 5 clip through dovi_reshape give 1.01
against vf_libplacebo.

Signed-off-by: lusoris <lusoris@proton.me>
---
 doc/filters.texi                   |   9 ++
 libavfilter/Makefile               |   5 +-
 libavfilter/opencl/bt2408_hable.cl | 195 +++++++++++++++++++++++++++++
 libavfilter/opencl_source.h        |   1 +
 libavfilter/vf_tonemap_opencl.c    |  73 ++++++++++-
 5 files changed, 276 insertions(+), 7 deletions(-)
 create mode 100644 libavfilter/opencl/bt2408_hable.cl

